<GPLPatch>

<!-- FFB: deepen the force curve's notch from -1.20 to -1.33.

This is what GEM's ffb3test1.xml was trying to do. That file writes 315 dwords
starting at the HEADER's address: 157 of them are the stock table misaligned by
four entries, 155 are byte-identical no-ops, and only three are real edits. The
misalignment overwrites the 5.0 domain max and the integer count 313, and moves
the curve's ascending limb while leaving the descending limb in place, breaking a
symmetry the whole table is built on.

This emits the stock curve with every NEGATIVE sample scaled by 1.108333 so the notch
reaches -1.33. Symmetry is preserved exactly, the header is untouched, the positive
lobe is unchanged, and there is no step at the zero crossing because the samples
there are ~0. 25 of 313 entries are written.
NOT A RATE FIX.
-->

   <BinaryPatch>
      <!-- y[145] -0.00806 -> -0.00893 -->
      <VirtualAddress>0x0055BCD0</VirtualAddress>
      <Data>6A5C12BC</Data>
   </BinaryPatch>

